.TH ZVM-UNINSTALL 1 "August 2026" "ZVM v0.9.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zvm-uninstall \- remove an installed Zig version
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zvm uninstall
.I version
.br
.B zvm rm
.I version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove the requested Zig installation from the ZVM base directory.
Version shorthand and aliases are resolved against locally installed versions.
.PP
Only a top-level installation directory containing a
.B zig
or
.B zig.exe
file can be removed.
Paths, reserved ZVM state names, and symbolic links are rejected.
Remove links to local builds yourself.
.PP
Removing the globally active installation also removes the
.I bin
link; use
.B zvm use
to select another installed version.
Per-shell links pointing at the removed installation must also be switched
to an installed version.
Unreferenced dedupe-store files are pruned after removal; files still shared
by other installations remain available.
.PP
If the requested version is not installed, ZVM reports that fact and lists the
installed versions.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
zvm uninstall 0.13.0
zvm rm .13
zvm rm stable
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zvm (1),
.BR zvm-install (1),
.BR zvm-list (1),
.BR zvm-alias (1),
.BR zvm-use (1),
.BR zvm-dedupe (1)
